  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 112.1pt, "the achievable enhancement in tunability.   ")
  #line-at(95.664pt, 130.1pt, "Recent advances in atomic-scale fabrication of artificial 2D materials with broken mirror symmetry ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 148.1pt, "known as Janus 2D materials")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(211.97pt, 144.62pt, "25,26")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(227.69pt, 148.1pt, ", like WSSe and MoSSe")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(333.07pt, 144.62pt, "27")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(340.03pt, 148.1pt, " give a possibility. The intrinsic broken ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 166.1pt, "mirror symmetry in the Janus monolayer can result in an out-of-plane dipole, which modifies the ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 184.1pt, "interlayer potential-energy landscape. This can lead to stronger out-of-plane interlayer interactions but ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 202.1pt, "lower interlayer friction and facilitate atomic reconstruction in the near-commensurate regime")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(479.74pt, 198.62pt, "28")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(486.7pt, 202.1pt, ". As a ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 220.1pt, "results, Janus-induced symmetry breaking modifies the twist-angle dependence of interlayer ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 238.1pt, "interactions, producing a rapid reduction and a pronounced minimum at small twist angles")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(484.3pt, 234.62pt, "29")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(491.26pt, 238.1pt, ". By ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 256.1pt, "altering both interlayer coupling and the reconstruction pathway of the moiré lattice, Janus ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 274.13pt, "functionalization provides an additional knob for enhancing control over interlayer phonon transport.  ")
  #line-at(95.664pt, 292.13pt, "In this work, we investigate TC in twisted MoSSe/MoS₂ by combining twist-angle control with ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 310.13pt, "Janus functionalization. Time-domain thermoreflectance (TDTR) method show that TC in ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 328.13pt, "MoSSe/MoS₂ is far more sensitive to twist angle than in bilayer MoS₂, reaching a minimum at small ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 346.13pt, "twist angles. Raman spectroscopy, density functional theory (DFT) calculations, and transmission ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 364.13pt, "electron microscopy (TEM) reveal enhanced interlayer sliding and atomic reconstruction, leading to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 382.13pt, "locally distorted aperiodic moiré patterns that drive the TC variation. This work advances the ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 400.13pt, "understanding of thermal transport in 2D moiré systems and demonstrates Janus functionalization as ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 418.13pt, "an effective phonon-engineering strategy. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 454.15pt, "High-quality Janus vdW fabrication and structural characterization ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.664pt, 472.15pt, "We fabricated twisted bilayer MoS")
